  "name": "AML Cytogenetics PANEL(KARYOTYPING + FISH)",
  "code": "1386",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"2114\" data-end=\"2464\">\n<li data-start=\"2114\" data-end=\"2323\">\n<p data-start=\"2116\" data-end=\"2323\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"2116\" data-end=\"2154\">Abnormal Karyotype / FISH Positive</strong>: Suggests presence of cytogenetic changes associated with <strong data-start=\"2213\" data-end=\"2245\">Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)</strong>. Used for <strong data-start=\"2256\" data-end=\"2269\">diagnosis</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2271\" data-end=\"2294\">risk stratification</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"2300\" data-end=\"2322\">treatment planning</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"2324\" data-end=\"2464\">\n<p data-start=\"2326\" data-end=\"2464\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"2326\" data-end=\"2343\">Normal Result</strong>: No chromosomal abnormalities detected. Does not rule out AML; molecular testing (e.g., FLT3, NPM1) may still be needed.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2473\" data-end=\"2655\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"2473\" data-end=\"2481\">Note</strong>: This test combines <strong data-start=\"2502\" data-end=\"2542\">classical cytogenetics (karyotyping)</strong> and <strong data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"2571\">targeted FISH probes</strong> to provide a comprehensive genetic profile in suspected or diagnosed <strong data-start=\"2641\" data-end=\"2648\">AML</strong> cases.</span></p>",
